A collection of 18 posters illustrating a series of scenes associated with New England. Scenes include: a scene of the Boston Tea Party and another depicting a firework display by a Massachusetts militia during the War of American Independence. Also includes views of Boston streets around the time of this famous event and of Washington's crossing of the Delaware. Some of these posters (such as those accompanying the Boston Tea party and Massachusetts militia scene) are accompanied by additional details concerning particular buildings in Boston and Cambridge.

The New England Regional Pastoral Association Poster Collection is a collection of over one hundred twenty-five pieces of original art and reproduction artwork acquired by New England Conservatory (NEC). The collection was created by Nancy Bohnsack from an estate sale in Fall River, Massachusetts. In 1974 Professor Thomas Mann founded a group of faculty and alumni to form The New England Regional Art Pastoral Association whose goal was to collect art relating to New England landscapes and architecture and to give these original artworks to deserving schools, museums and churches.

